{"id":"b4b5a78ced8d341e","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-thm-thom-isomorphism.md","title":"Thom Isomorphism Theorem","display":"thm-thom-isomorphism — Thom Isomorphism Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-thom-isomorphism","aliases":["58-thm-thom-isomorphism"],"display":"thm-thom-isomorphism — Thom Isomorphism Theorem","depends_on":[]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-thom-isomorphism"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-thom-isomorphism</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-thom-isomorphism — Thom Isomorphism Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<span class=\"property-null\">无</span>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R,B,E,\\pi,n,U\\in V\">\\(R,B,E,\\pi,n,U\\in V\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{CommutativeRing}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(R)\">\\(\\operatorname{CommutativeRing}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(R)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ParacompactHausdorff}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(B)\">\\(\\operatorname{ParacompactHausdorff}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(B)\\)</span> have their standard meanings</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ROrientedRealVectorBundle}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\pi,E,B,n;R)\">\\(\\operatorname{ROrientedRealVectorBundle}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\pi,E,B,n;R)\\)</span> denotes a rank-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> real vector bundle equipped with an <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span>-orientation</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ThomIsomorphismData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(U;\\pi,E,B,n,R)\">\\(\\operatorname{ThomIsomorphismData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(U;\\pi,E,B,n,R)\\)</span> means that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\\in H^n(E,E\\setminus s[B];R)\">\\(U\\in H^n(E,E\\setminus s[B];R)\\)</span> is the corresponding Thom class and cup product with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> gives <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H^k(B;R)\\cong H^{k+n}(E,E\\setminus s[B];R)\">\\(H^k(B;R)\\cong H^{k+n}(E,E\\setminus s[B];R)\\)</span> for every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\in\\mathbb Z\">\\(k\\in\\mathbb Z\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}thom\\text{-}isomorphism}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{CommutativeRing}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(R)\n\\land n\\in\\omega\n\\land\\operatorname{ParacompactHausdorff}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(B)\n\\land\\operatorname{ROrientedRealVectorBundle}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\pi,E,B,n;R)\n\\to\\exists U\\in V\\;\n\\operatorname{ThomIsomorphismData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(U;\\pi,E,B,n,R).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}thom\\text{-}isomorphism}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{CommutativeRing}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(R)\n\\land n\\in\\omega\n\\land\\operatorname{ParacompactHausdorff}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(B)\n\\land\\operatorname{ROrientedRealVectorBundle}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\pi,E,B,n;R)\n\\to\\exists U\\in V\\;\n\\operatorname{ThomIsomorphismData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(U;\\pi,E,B,n,R).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The chosen <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span>-orientation determines the Thom class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span>, whose restriction to each fiber is the preferred generator.</li>\n<li>The available vector-bundle atom does not encode <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span>-orientations, and the available cohomology atom only forms the quotient of an already supplied cochain complex; it does not define singular cohomology of spaces or pairs, pullback, cup product, relative groups, or module isomorphisms.  The theorem is therefore explicitly metatheoretic instead of applying that generic quotient predicate as though it supplied all of these constructions.</li>\n<li>Thom–Pontryagin construction: bordism <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leftrightarrow\">\\(\\leftrightarrow\\)</span> homology.</li>\n<li>Cobordism ring <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega_*\">\\(\\Omega_*\\)</span> computed via Thom spectra.</li>\n<li>Equivalently, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\widetilde H^{k+n}(Th(\\pi);R)\\cong H^k(B;R)\">\\(\\widetilde H^{k+n}(Th(\\pi);R)\\cong H^k(B;R)\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[],"math":[{"tex":"R,B,E,\\pi,n,U\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{CommutativeRing}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(R)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ParacompactHausdorff}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(B)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ROrientedRealVectorBundle}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\pi,E,B,n;R)","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"R","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ThomIsomorphismData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(U;\\pi,E,B,n,R)","display":false},{"tex":"U\\in H^n(E,E\\setminus s[B];R)","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"H^k(B;R)\\cong H^{k+n}(E,E\\setminus s[B];R)","display":false},{"tex":"k\\in\\mathbb Z","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}thom\\text{-}isomorphism}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\operatorname{CommutativeRing}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(R)\n\\land n\\in\\omega\n\\land\\operatorname{ParacompactHausdorff}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(B)\n\\land\\operatorname{ROrientedRealVectorBundle}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\pi,E,B,n;R)\n\\to\\exists U\\in V\\;\n\\operatorname{ThomIsomorphismData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(U;\\pi,E,B,n,R).","display":true},{"tex":"R","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"R","display":false},{"tex":"\\leftrightarrow","display":false},{"tex":"\\Omega_*","display":false},{"tex":"\\widetilde H^{k+n}(Th(\\pi);R)\\cong H^k(B;R)","display":false}],"bytes":2015,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4461","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-thm-thom-isomorphism.md|58-thm-thom-isomorphism]]（batch03）"}],"outgoing":[]}